<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7862" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">chorda</span></b> , ae, f., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χορδή</span>. * <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>An intestine</i>, <i>as food</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Petr. 66, 7</span></i> (al. leg.
			cord.).— Far more freq., </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Catgut</i>, <i>a string</i> (<i>of a musical instrument</i>), <i><span class="en">Cic. de
				Or. 3, 57, 214</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. N. D.
				2, 59, 149 <i>fin.</i></span></i>; <i><span class="en">Lucr. 2,
			412</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 505</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Tib.
				2, 5, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 4,
				70</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 4, 9, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. S. 1, 3,
				8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. A. P. 348
			al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A rope</i>, <i>cord</i>, for binding
			a slave: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tunc tibi actutum chorda tenditur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Most. 3, 2, 55</span></i>
			 Lorenz.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
